WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- All right, y'all.
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.210
We have time for one more story

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:04.109
on this Martin Luther King Jr. Day,

00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:05.485
and it's a really important one.

00:00:05.485 --> 00:00:06.904
This is What I'm Liking.
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.904 --> 00:00:08.857
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.857 --> 00:00:11.370
It's easy to think the life and legacy

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.860
of Martin Luther King
Jr. are the distant past,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.240
but that's not the case.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.690
Today marks what would've
been his 94th birthday

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.030
and his work continues to this day.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.350
To emphasize that point,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.320
his only grandchild is still a teenager.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.550
She's also an activist

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.650
and author, just like her grandfather.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.260
Her latest children's book
is, "We Dream a World".

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.660
Here to talk about it,
is Yolanda Renee King.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.584
Give it up.

00:00:34.584 --> 00:00:36.248
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:37.702
Hello!

00:00:37.702 --> 00:00:39.060
- Hi!

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.970
- Welcome to the show and
congratulations on this.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.160
This is such a cool achievement.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.070
- Thank you so much and
thank you for having me.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.620
- Absolutely, so tell us about the book.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.300
- So the book is...

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.950
Well it's a children's book,

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.180
and it's inspired

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.740
by the late Langston Hughes'
poem, "We Dream a World",

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.750
which actually, interestingly enough,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.910
inspired the "I Have a Dream" speech.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.860
And it really shows, using imagery

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.203
and poetic language, the type of world

00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:09.990
that we can have and the type of world

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:11.580
that I think we talk about so much,

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.410
but we forget what that looks like.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.650
And so, I think that this
book will really give kids

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:21.150
and really honestly, families,
a visual of the type of world

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:21.990
that we can have.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.330
- Absolutely, we always
need reminders, right?

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.650
Absolutely.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.700
- So how do you plan

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.040
to honor your grandfather's legacy today?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.830
- So our organization,
my family's organization,

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.210
the Drum Major Institute,

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:34.650
we're actually working

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.830
on launching our service initiative today.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.400
Because five years from
now, for the 100th birthday,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.270
we are trying to obtain 100 million hours

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.620
of service across the nation.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.580
So today is the launch of
our new service initiative.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.568
- That's incredible!
(audience applauding)

00:01:52.568 --> 00:01:53.713
Well, Yolanda's latest book,

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.430
"We Dream a World", is available right now

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.680
and everyone is going home with a copy!

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.811
You're all getting one.

00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:00.792
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:00.792 --> 00:02:02.605
Thank you so much, Yolanda.

00:02:02.605 --> 00:02:05.336
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:05.336 --> 00:02:06.300
And that's not all.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.523
Our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:08.523 --> 00:02:10.710
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.810
support the ongoing work of your family.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.000
So they're gonna be writing
the Drum Major Institute

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.740
a check for $1000 just to help out.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:17.604
How does that sound?

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:18.595
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:18.595 --> 00:02:20.096
- Thank you.

00:02:20.096 --> 00:02:21.880
- Thank you so much, Yolanda!

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.650
Thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.082
Cynthia Erivo, Amel Amin,

00:02:26.082 --> 00:02:29.430
Coleman Woodson Jr. and Kings Return.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.455
Have a good day, y'all,

00:02:30.455 --> 00:02:32.205
and if it's not, try and change it.

